WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:05.000
Every new machine starts the same way. You type the same long command, again.

00:05.000 --> 00:09.800
It lives in a note, a chat, a gist, or your shell history.

00:10.400 --> 00:15.000
ForgeHub is a home for your shell commands. Paste yours on the web, name it, save it.

00:15.000 --> 00:19.800
Text only, versioned, and private by default.

00:20.400 --> 00:25.000
Log in once from the terminal. Then just type fg and the name.

00:25.000 --> 00:29.800
ForgeHub shows exactly what it will run, and asks you first.

00:30.300 --> 00:33.300
Safety is the product. Other people's snippets need a typed yes.

00:33.600 --> 00:36.600
If a snippet changed, you see the diff first.

00:36.900 --> 00:39.800
With no terminal, it refuses to run.

00:40.400 --> 00:45.000
Keep snippets private, share a link, or publish them.

00:45.000 --> 00:49.800
Search, star and fork. Record in your terminal and push like git.

00:50.500 --> 00:56.000
ForgeHub. Save a command once. Run it anywhere.

00:56.000 --> 00:59.500
Save a command once. Run it anywhere with fg.
